// Re-exports its own submodule. 'pub' comes first, as it does on every
// declaration and fold: 'pub use inner;' makes each public name of inner a public
// name of facade, reached by a path from the parent and imported by a sister.
// inner itself stays private to facade.

mod facade;

// A global whose type is Panel, which only the 'use' below brings. A module's
// folds run in a fixed order -- the imports, the globals, then the standalone
// 'use's -- so this global's fold WAITS in the first fold pass, and is made in
// the next, with the re-export of area it makes. reader, a sister, wildcard-
// imports this module, and takes area in that next pass too. Imports form a DAG, so
// this, not a loop, is what the repeated fold passes are for (modFoldAll).
pub mut panel Panel = Panel[3i64, 4i64] pub use area;

pub use inner;
